# Byte-compiled caches are build artefacts, never committed evidence.
#
# This matters for more than tidiness here. The workflow's "Enforce team scope"
# step inspects `git status --porcelain -uall`, so ANY file a run leaves behind
# outside this team's write scope fails the job. Importing the accepted package
# at `frontier/frontier_query_concept_recall/` writes `__pycache__/*.pyc` there,
# and that path is OUT of the scope guard for a team id containing hyphens
# (defect B). A stray .pyc would therefore fail the team step for a reason that
# has nothing to do with the work.
#
# Run every entry point with:
#     PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=frontier python ...
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
